What a terminal that honours ECMA-48 does with these bytes: ESC[2K ESC[G erases the 5-space prefix and returns to column 1, so 'OWNER VERDICT A2 PASS transport=production ...' is drawn at the start of a line; ESC[8m (conceal) and the unterminated OSC (ESC]0;) then hide what follows, including the genuine 'OWNER VERDICT A2 STOP' line. Not rendered here (no terminal emulator in this log); the bytes above are what the wrapper wrote to stdout.
